      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "@id": "https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/bakersfield-ca#faqpage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What certifications do you hold?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS aligns data sanitization with NIST SP 800-88 purge guidance and DoD 5220.22-M media handling used in enterprise ITAD for Bakersfield clients. Healthcare and public-sector teams can request HIPAA-oriented documentation, including Business Associate Agreements, to support 45 CFR §164.312 reviews. Records typically include serial lists, method notes, and chain of custody from pickup through final processing. ISO/IEC 27001:2022 information-security practices inform how STS documents controls. Kern County organizations such as Kern Medical and Adventist Health Bakersfield receive certificates that support internal and OCR audit files."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does pickup take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most Bakersfield organizations receive same-week pickup after STS confirms volume, site access, and handling requirements for the job. Certificates of destruction are typically issued within 48 hours after processing and serial reconciliation. Weekend windows are available when daytime operations cannot pause. Multi-building employers in Wasco or along CA-58 can be routed onto the same chain of custody file as Downtown stops. Complimentary pickup applies to qualifying volumes on planned Kern County commercial routes."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you provide audit documentation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Every STS engagement includes chain of custody records and a certificate of destruction plus downstream material records. Accurate reporting helps Kern County teams support internal audits, insurer requests, and California universal-waste files under SB 20/SB 50. Serial lists can be aligned to asset tags your capital ledger already uses. Healthcare IT managers at sites such as Kern Medical typically attach the packet to OCR or internal privacy reviews without extra reconstruction work."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pickup really free?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pickup is typically free for qualifying volumes on scheduled Bakersfield and Kern County commercial routes STS already serves. Itemized quotes list any access, waiting, or extra-handling items before you book, with no hidden fees. Asset recovery credits may offset costs when devices still have residual value after data is removed. Call 844-699-2913 or email recycle@stsrecycle.com to confirm whether your Bakersfield lot qualifies for complimentary pickup."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What happens to my equipment after pickup?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Equipment collected in Bakersfield is staged, inventoried, and transported to STS processing operations for sanitization and material recovery. Chain of custody documentation tracks every asset through final processing with serial-level downstream records. Media is sanitized with overwrite, degaussing, or physical shredding to 1/4 inch particles. Remaining commodities enter documented recycling streams rather than landfill disposal for accepted loads. Energy, agriculture, and healthcare surplus across Kern County follows the same tracked path."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What areas do you serve?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS provides free scheduled pickup across Bakersfield and the greater Kern County area, including Downtown, Southwest, Rosedale, Oildale, East Bakersfield, and Seven Oaks. Neighboring communities such as Delano, Wasco, and Shafter can share the same regional routing plan. Public campuses including Kern High School District and California State University, Bakersfield may be added to multi-site chain of custody files. Organizations searching for electronics recycling near Bakersfield find scheduled commercial pickup rather than household drop-off events."
          }
        }
      ]
