          "name": "What certifications and standards do you reference?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS uses documented processes that support responsible electronics handling and data protection. Service discussions may include NIST SP 800-88 Rev. 2 guidance, HIPAA considerations for protected health information, and DoD 5220.22-M references where appropriate to the project."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What areas do you serve around Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS serves Bakersfield and the greater Kern County area for qualifying business, institutional, and organizational projects. Organizations searching for electronics recycling near me throughout Bakersfield can request scheduled pickup for offices, campuses, warehouses, healthcare organizations, and industrial operations."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does business pickup take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Many projects can be scheduled on a same-week basis after equipment volume and site requirements are reviewed. Larger projects, multi-building collections, or jobs requiring detailed asset tracking may need additional coordination before a pickup date is confirmed."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you provide audit documentation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS can provide chain of custody records and project documentation based on the services requested. Organizations with data-bearing assets can discuss serial tracking, data destruction records, and reporting expectations before equipment is collected."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pickup free for Bakersfield organizations?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pickup is free for qualifying volumes. Eligibility depends on the equipment mix, quantity, access conditions, and project location. Contact STS with an inventory summary so the team can confirm the appropriate pickup approach for your organization."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What happens to electronics after pickup?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Equipment enters a managed processing workflow that can include sorting, data handling, material recovery, and downstream reporting. The service plan is tailored to the equipment type and the documentation requirements established before collection."
          }
        }
